# 27. DEVELOPMENT RULES

1. Inspect the existing project before making changes.
2. Do not destroy existing functionality without justification.
3. Maintain a working application throughout development.
4. Build features incrementally.
5. Do not generate fake functionality.
6. Do not leave core features as placeholders.
7. Use real data persistence.
8. Implement validation.
9. Use reusable components.
10. Keep code modular.
11. Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
12. Avoid unnecessary complexity.
13. Keep the UI consistent.
14. Test features after implementation.
15. Fix errors before proceeding.
16. Maintain documentation.
17. Explain important architectural decisions.
18. Do not claim unfinished functionality is completed.
19. Do not silently remove features.
20. Do not replace a working application with a mockup.
21. Use database migrations.
22. Ensure desktop and web versions share compatible business logic.
23. Enforce permissions at the backend.
24. Implement proper loading, error, success and empty states.
25. Ensure the application can be built and run locally.
26. Do not create or implement any ticketing or helpdesk features.
27. Keep the application focused on IT operations and asset management.

